From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guillaume Thouvenin <guillaume.thouvenin@vates.tech>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 14:43:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Release leftover HA static VDIs when HA is disabled at
 startup

This patch fixes an issue where the HA statefile and metadata VDIs remain
attached to dom0 after a host restart, even if HA has been disabled on the
pool. Here is the scenario:
- HA is enabled on the pool
- A host is fenced, so it is shut down
- HA is disabled on the pool. ha_release_resources is called on live hosts but
  the fenced one doesn't receive the cleanup and keeps the statefile and
  metadata VDIs in /etc/xensource/static-vdis
- The fenced host restarts:
  - Its local database still has ha.armed set to true, so on_server_restart
    attached the static VDIs and tries to start the HA daemon
  - ha_start_daemon fails with MTC_EXIT_INVALID_POOL_STATE because the pool is
    no longer in HA mode. While failing, it sets ha.armed to false in the local
    database without releasing the static VDIs
  - Later resynchronise_ha_state sees HA disabled on both localhost and the
    pool. So the (true, false) case, which normally calls ha_release_resources,
    is not taken and no cleanup is done.
At the end of the boot, the statefile and the metadata VDIs are still attached
to dom0 and must be removed manually with "static-vdis detach/del".

So the patch adds release_local_ha_static_vdis that deactivates and detaches
any HA statefile or metadata VDI still configured as a static VDI on the host,
and calls it in the (false, false) case of resynchronise_ha_state. When nothing
is left behind it does nothing.

ha_release_resources now also uses this helper. It used
Db.Pool.get_ha_statefiles to find statefiles, but a statefile attached on the
host always has a local static-vdis entry, so the local configuration is what
this host actually need to release. Metadata VDIs were already found using the
local configuration. Xha_metadata_vdi.deactivate_and_detach_existing is no
longer used and is removed.

Tracking-reference: XCPNG-3914
Signed-off-by: Guillaume Thouvenin <guillaume.thouvenin@vates.tech>
(cherry picked from commit ac2246af7b555be217bd8246c7e4c35aaf998b2a)
